1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,650
If your interviewer ever asks,

2
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:04,930
"What is your greatest weakness?"...

3
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:06,640
do not tell the truth.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,580
Do not tell them about yourself.

5
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:11,980
Never say you have no questions.

6
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:13,470
And never wait for them

7
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,620
to get back to you.

8
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:17,900
This is Instruction 444.

9
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,170
There are four rules.

10
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:21,880
Follow them exactly.

11
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:23,450
Otherwise, you will have

12
00:00:23,470 --> 00:00:25,660
to activate the emergency protocol.

13
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:27,540
Rule one.

14
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:30,080
Do not tell them about yourself.

15
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:31,980
"Tell me about yourself."

16
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:34,300
They have already read your résumé.

17
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:35,870
Three times.

18
00:00:35,890 --> 00:00:37,050
Every page.

19
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,990
They are not asking who you are.

20
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,880
They are checking which version of you

21
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,810
is safe to let out of the room.

22
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:45,350
Smile.

23
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:46,870
Say your name.

24
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:49,430
Say one sentence about your last job.

25
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:50,540
Then stop.

26
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:53,280
Do not mention your hobbies.

27
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,400
Do not mention your family.

28
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:57,160
Do not say where you live.

29
00:00:57,610 --> 00:01:00,100
The last candidate said she lived alone.

30
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:02,240
The interviewer wrote it down.

31
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:04,470
Then he underlined it.

32
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:07,450
Rule two.

33
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,580
Do not tell the truth.

34
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:12,520
Then the one in the middle leans forward.

35
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:15,270
"What is your greatest weakness?"

36
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:17,410
The room goes quiet.

37
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,930
The air conditioner stops.

38
00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:21,630
Even the clock waits.

39
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,970
Only two answers are allowed.

40
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:26,570
"I work too hard."

41
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,420
"I care too much."

42
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:31,320
Do not say procrastination.

43
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:33,680
Do not say public speaking.

44
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,770
Do not say you get nervous.

45
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,230
Whatever you say becomes your weakness.

46
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:40,350
Forever.

47
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:41,907
It goes in your file,

48
00:01:41,927 --> 00:01:43,590
and the file follows you.

49
00:01:44,340 --> 00:01:47,490
A candidate once said, "I can't say no."

50
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:50,630
He has worked there for nine years.

51
00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:52,320
He has never gone home.

52
00:01:54,170 --> 00:01:55,620
Rule three.

53
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:58,160
Do not say you have no questions.

54
00:01:58,610 --> 00:02:01,020
At the end, they put their pens down.

55
00:02:01,490 --> 00:02:03,310
"Do you have any questions for us?"

56
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,530
Never say no.

57
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:06,620
In this room,

58
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,440
the interview only ends when you ask something.

59
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,110
Say, "No, I think you covered everything," and

60
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:15,490
the clock on the wall goes back to nine.

61
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,330
The one in the middle tilts his head.

62
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,650
"Then let's start again.

63
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:22,020
Tell me about yourself."

64
00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:25,560
One candidate said no three times.

65
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:27,440
He is still in that room.

66
00:02:27,510 --> 00:02:30,560
For him, it is still Monday, nine A.M.

67
00:02:32,410 --> 00:02:34,660
Do not ask about the salary.

68
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:36,390
Do not ask what happened to

69
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:38,170
the last person in this role.

70
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,390
Ask only this.

71
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:41,870
"When will I hear back?"

72
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,730
Rule four.

73
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,370
Emergency protocol.

74
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,910
How to fight back.

75
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,570
They stand up.

76
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:50,020
"We'll get back to you."

77
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,880
They mean it.

78
00:02:51,990 --> 00:02:54,560
At three A.M., you wake up.

79
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:56,530
Three interviewers are standing at

80
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:57,680
the foot of your bed.

81
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:00,550
"We have a few more questions."

82
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,630
Here is what does not work.

83
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,930
Pretending to be asleep.

84
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:09,380
They write down, "Lacks enthusiasm."

85
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:12,240
Saying you already took another offer.

86
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:14,600
They ask for the company's name.

87
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:16,860
Then they visit that company too.

88
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:19,160
Blocking their email.

89
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:20,450
The next email comes

90
00:03:20,470 --> 00:03:22,140
from inside your house.

91
00:03:23,890 --> 00:03:26,420
There is only one thing that works.

92
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:27,480
Interview them.

93
00:03:27,930 --> 00:03:28,740
Sit up.

94
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,580
Fold your hands.

95
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:32,860
Look the middle one in the eye.

96
00:03:33,050 --> 00:03:34,060
"So.

97
00:03:34,170 --> 00:03:36,240
What is your greatest weakness?"

98
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:39,910
The rules of that room apply to them too.

99
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:41,200
They cannot lie.

100
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:43,310
The first one says,

101
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:45,470
"Being asked questions."

102
00:03:45,490 --> 00:03:46,700
He gets smaller.

103
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,050
"Tell me about yourself."

104
00:03:49,070 --> 00:03:51,000
The second one starts to shake.

105
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:52,920
There is nothing to tell.

106
00:03:53,310 --> 00:03:54,530
He gets smaller.

107
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:56,350
And the last question.

108
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:58,300
"Why should I hire you?"

109
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:01,400
Nobody has ever asked them that.

110
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:03,290
They fold up like paper,

111
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:05,210
and slide out under your door.

112
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,610
One week later, an email.

113
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:10,560
"We regret to inform you

114
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,960
that our interviewers have resigned.

115
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,280
Would you like the position?"

116
00:04:14,730 --> 00:04:15,910
Job title:

117
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:16,980
Interviewer.

118
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:18,230
Location:

119
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:19,070
the chair.

120
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:23,510
And that was Instruction 444.

121
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,500
If this ever happens to you...

122
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,860
you know the protocol.
